  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The dataset is limited to content explicitly self-tagged by users with a single hashtag, which may bias the sample toward specific types of disclosures.",
      "what": "A mixed-methods analysis evaluated 190 TikTok videos carrying the hashtag harassment alongside 66,337 associated comments to categorize types of harassment and analyze comment stances. Qualitative coding classified videos into seven distinct forms of abuse, finding that while sexual harassment was the most frequent topic, stalking-related content generated the highest view counts. Statistical modeling of psycholinguistic features showed that sexual harassment posts prompted strong victim solidarity, whereas posts detailing law enforcement harassment triggered systemic critique.",
      "why": "It demonstrates that engagement on short-form video platforms varies significantly by the type of abuse depicted, countering the assumption that content frequency correlates directly with audience reach."
    }
  },
